This directory contains the generated configs from the dump_configs.yml playbook


To generate them, there are three options:

- In any Iris pull request, we can click on the build, then in the "Summary" section in
  the "Related" column, we see "1 published". Click on this, then either download an
  individual config file, or all the config files together in a zip file.


- Locally, it's easiest to run this with the dynamic backends disabled, like this:

  ```
  ansible-playbook -i data/instances ansible/dump_configs.yml -eenable_dynamic_backends= -esimulation=
  ```

  The `-eenable_dynamic_backends=` turns off processing of dynamic backends, which are
  stored in Ceph, so processing them would need Ceph credentials and roles from Dante.

  The `-esimulation=` specifies that we want production (not simulation) configs.

  The configs will be dumped into this directory.


- Alternately, we can set up the imported Dante roles and the Ceph access, then run:

  ```
  ansible-playbook -i data/instances ansible/dump_configs.yml -esimulation=
  ```


Note that the configs in this directory are **not used for anything**; they're purely
for human review.
